<instruction name="VCVTNEPS2BF16">
 <copyright>Copyright (C) Intel Corporation. All Rights Reserved.</copyright>
 <shortdesc>Convert Packed Single Data to Packed BF16 Data</shortdesc>
 <longdesc><para unique="1046493">
   <string>This instruction loads packed FP32 elements from a SIMD register or memory, converts the elements to BF16, and writes the result to the destination SIMD register.</string></para>
  <para unique="1046494">
   <string>The upper bits of the destination register beyond the down-converted BF16 elements are zeroed.</string></para>
  <para unique="1046495">
   <string>This instruction uses &#8220;Round to nearest (even)&#8221; rounding mode. Output denormals are always flushed to zero and input denormals are always treated as zero. MXCSR is not consulted nor updated.</string></para>
  <para unique="1045972">
   <string>As the instruction operand encoding table shows, the EVEX.vvvv field is not used for encoding an operand. EVEX.vvvv is reserved and must be 0b1111 otherwise instructions will #UD.</string></para>
  </longdesc>
